msgstr "Direktorijas un failu sistēmas"

#. (itstool) path: section/para
#: C/goscaja.xml:1052
msgid ""
"In Linux and other Unix-like operating systems, the filesystem is organised "
"in a hierarchical, tree-like structure. The highest level of the filesystem "
"is the <filename>/</filename> or <emphasis>root directory</emphasis>. These "
"operating systems create a virtual file system, in which a filesystem "
"object, such as a file or a directory, is represented by an inode. Each "
"inode stores information about its parent and children, as well as its own "
"attributes, among others, the owner, the permissions, the last change, "
"access or modification of the filesystem object."
msgstr ""
"Linux un citās Unix tipa operētājsistēmās failu sistēma ir sakārtota "
"hierarhiskā, kokam līdzīgā struktūrā. Failu sistēmas augstākais līmenis ir "
"<filename>/</filename> jeb <emphasis>saknes direktorija</emphasis>. Šīs "
"operētājsistēmas veido virtuālu failu sistēmu, kurā katru failu sistēmas "
"objektu, piemēram, failu vai direktoriju, attēlo i-mezgls. Katrs i-mezgls "
"glabā informāciju par savu vecākobjektu un pēcnācējiem, kā arī savus "
"atribūtus, tostarp īpašnieku, atļaujas un failu sistēmas objekta pēdējās "
"izmaiņas, piekļuves vai modificēšanas laiku."

#. (itstool) path: section/para
#: C/goscaja.xml:1054
msgid ""
"For example, <filename>/home/jebediah/cheeses.odt</filename> shows the "
"correct full path to the <filename>cheeses.odt</filename> file that exists "
"in the <filename>jebediah</filename> directory which is under the "
"<filename>home</filename> directory, which in turn, is under the root "
"(<filename>/</filename>) directory."
msgstr ""
